  "result": "Found Craven 2002, Yuan 2005, Danilatos 1990, Tang 2006, Meredith 2006, Oho 2007. Need to gather evidence from these.",
  "evaluation": null
}"}

{"plan_objective_id": 1, "updated_plan_objective_json": "{
  "id": 1,
  "objective": "Search for literature on VP-SEM/ESEM charge neutralization mechanism and principles",
  "rationale": "Need peer-reviewed sources explaining gas ionization charge neutralization, pressure ranges, gas types, detector types for Q1",
  "status": "completed",
  "result": "Found extensive evidence from Craven 2002, Tang 2006, Danilatos 1988, 1990, Staniewicz 2012, Alasmari 2021. Charge neutralization occurs via gas ionization by SE/BSE/PE, positive ion drift to negatively charged surface. Steady state potential reduces from kV-scale to ~0 V or slightly positive. PLAs and differential pumping described. GSED replaces ET detector.",
  "evaluation": "All aspects of Q1 covered with peer-reviewed evidence."
}"}

{"plan_objective_id": 2, "updated_plan_objective_json": "{
  "id": 2,
  "objective": "Search for literature on gas scattering / beam skirt effects on quantitative EDS in VP-SEM",
  "rationale": "Need sources on beam skirt radius, scattered fraction, effects on k-ratio quantification, especially at low kV like 5 keV for Q3",
  "status": "completed",
  "result": "Found Le Berre 2007, Carlton 2006, Arnoult 2011, Khouchaf 2011, Mansour 2020, Danilatos 1988. Beam skirt fraction = exp(-m) unscattered, skirt extends hundreds of µm. At 5 kV scattering greatly increased. Corrections (Gauvin extrapolation) achieve ~2% of 0 Pa at 30 kV. Helium reduces skirt. No validation of accurate k-ratio quantitation at 5 kV in VP mode found.",
  "evaluation": "Q3 extensively covered with published data and correction methods."
}"}

{"plan_objective_id": 3, "updated_plan_objective_json": "{
  "id": 3,
  "objective": "Find and evaluate the candidate recommended papers (Danilatos 1988, Thiel & Toth 2005, Newbury 2002, Stokes 2008) for Q2",
  "rationale": "Need to evaluate these specific papers to recommend the best single introductory reference",
  "status": "completed",
  "result": "Newbury 2002 (J. Res. NIST 107:567-603) is the best recommendation for the user's application. It specifically addresses X-ray microanalysis in VP-SEM/ESEM, covers beam skirt effects and quantitative EDS issues, and is freely available as a NIST government publication (no copyright). Danilatos 1988 is foundational but focuses on ESEM theory broadly, not X-ray microanalysis. Thiel & Toth 2005 covers imaging contrast, not microanalysis. Stokes 2008 is a book (not freely accessible).",
  "evaluation": "The Newbury 2002 paper is the best match given the user's focus on quantitative X-ray microanalysis in VP-SEM."
}"}

{"plan_objective_id": 4, "updated_plan_objective_json": "{
  "id": 4,
  "objective": "Search for vendor-specific VP-SEM information, especially Apreo low-vacuum capabilities, and other vendor naming conventions for Q4",
  "rationale": "Need information about Thermo Fisher Apreo low-vacuum mode, Zeiss VP, Hitachi VP-SEM naming and pressure ranges",
  "status": "completed",
  "result": "Found: FEI Quanta has 3 modes - high vacuum, low vacuum (10-2000 Pa), ESEM (10-4000 Pa). FEI/ElectroScan ESEM reaches ~20 Torr (2666 Pa). VP-SEMs typically ~300 Pa (2 Torr). Mohan 1998 confirms VP-SEM up to ~2 Torr/300 Pa. Hitachi S-3000N is a VP-SEM used in Le Berre 2007. Konopova 2023 mentions Apreo SEM with volumescope but describes usage mainly in high vacuum. Limited published peer-reviewed literature specifically about Apreo low-vacuum specs; must note this honestly.",
  "evaluation": "Vendor naming and pressure ranges covered from available literature. Apreo-specific published data is limited."
}"}

{"plan_objective_id": 5, "updated_plan_objective_json": "{
  "id": 5,
  "objective": "Search for Goldstein et al. textbook content on VP-SEM and quantitative EDS",
  "rationale": "The user specifically mentions this textbook as an authoritative source",
  "status": "completed",
  "result": "Found Goldstein et al. 2018 (4th ed., Springer, DOI 10.1007/978-1-4939-6676-9). Chapter 20 on k-ratio quantitative analysis. Chapter 12 on VP-SEM (DOI 10.1007/978-1-4939-6676-9_12) and Chapter 25 on attempting X-ray microanalysis in VP-SEM (DOI 10.1007/978-1-4939-6676-9_25) were listed as unobtainable but are referenced. The textbook confirms all analysis used carbon-coated specimens and Faraday cup beam current measurement.",
  "evaluation": "Goldstein et al. textbook identified with chapter-level DOIs for VP-SEM and quantitative EDS."
}"}

{"plan_objective_id": 6, "updated_plan_objective_json": "{
  "id": 6,
  "objective": "Gather and synthesize all evidence, create artifacts, and submit final answer",
  "rationale": "Need to compile all findings into a comprehensive answer addressing all 4 questions",
  "status": "in-progress",
  "result": "Artifacts created. Ready to submit final answer.",
  "evaluation": null
}"}

